  "romaji": "tokasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to comb (hair); to run a comb through",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to comb (hair); to run a comb or brush through",
      "explanation": "To pass a comb or brush through hair to untangle and smooth it. Written {梳|と}かす in kanji, but the kana spelling is far more common in everyday writing."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28246_tokasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{髪|かみ}をとかす。",
      "english": "To comb one's hair.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28246_tokasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{鏡|かがみ}の{前|まえ}で{髪|かみ}をとかした。",
      "english": "I combed my hair in front of the mirror.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28246_tokasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{出|で}かける{前|まえ}に、ブラシで{丁寧|ていねい}に{髪|かみ}をとかしておいた。",
      "english": "Before going out, I carefully combed my hair with a brush.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Almost always written in kana. The object is nearly always {髪|かみ} (hair).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}).\n- Pattern: {髪|かみ}をとかす\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {髪|かみ}をとかす: comb one's hair\n- くしでとかす: comb with a comb\n- ブラシでとかす: brush through\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {溶|と}かす: to melt; to dissolve — same reading but a different verb (heat or liquid). Context makes the meaning clear.",
